Title: HEX SUPPORT: TILL DEATH
Credit: a short film adapted from
Author: the gamebook Hex Support
Source: by Nikhil Math
Draft date: October 31, 2026
Notes: The shortest route to the Till Death ending: Off and On Again, Mama?, Law of the Dead, What Doris Wants, Team Plonk, Doris's Grave, Till Death. Written for two locations, three actors on camera and a weekend shoot. See production-notes.md.

FADE IN:

INT. STAIRWELL - DAWN

A narrow stone stairwell, spiralling up forever. THE TECH (30s, Hex Support polo, lanyard, the face of someone who has done this before) climbs, holding a paper cup of coffee.

A hand-painted sign on the wall: STAIR 412 OF 900.

The Tech stops. Breathes. Sips the coffee. Grimaces. It's lukewarm.

The Tech keeps climbing.

INT. WIZARD TOWER - CONTINUOUS

A cluttered round room. Candles, scrolls, a dusty mead barrel, a desk buried in junk. On a velvet cushion sits THE ORB: a frosted glass globe, glowing a sick, flickering blue.

PLONK THE WIZARD (900, looks every day of it, robe, enormous beard) jabs a crusty finger at it. Over his shoulders hangs the SILVERLIGHT CAPE, shimmering and faintly humming, done up with a ridiculous number of little padlocks.

The Tech arrives in the doorway, wheezing.

PLONK
This piece of shit stopped working the second I updated it.

The Tech raises a hand: one second. Still wheezing.

PLONK (CONT'D)
I have a meeting at 8 with my dead wife and her lawyer about our assets for the divorce. God, even in death this bitch ruins my life.

The orb flickers. A tiny, tired VOICE from inside it:

ORB (V.O.)
Please... kill me.

The Tech looks at the orb. The orb looks at the Tech. A long, knowing moment between two professionals.

The Tech sets the coffee down, turns the orb over, finds a little rune on the back, and holds a thumb on it.

TECH
(counting under breath)
...eight, nine, ten.

The glow dies.

Plonk GASPS like the Tech just drowned a kitten.

A beat. The orb blinks back to life, a soft, warm pink. A new VOICE, babyish and gurgling:

ORB (V.O.)
Ba?

PLONK
No. No no no.
(rounding on the Tech)
I have raised this orb since it was a baby. I got to go through the fucking puberty stage again?!

TECH
Is it working, though?

Plonk glares. Then, grudgingly, he leans over the orb.

PLONK
Well, hey, can you do Wizcast? I need to do a meeting.
(to the orb, slowly)
Are you smart enough for that?

The orb chimes. Plonk props a LAPTOP up behind it. On the screen:

ON SCREEN (WIZCAST)

DORIS (dead 40 years, half-decayed, pearls, perfect hair on the half that still has hair) sits in a dark room. Beside her, MARROW, a skeleton in a tie, with a briefcase and a tiny hourglass.

BACK TO SCENE

The Tech leans into frame, polite.

TECH
Uh, ma'am, the meeting isn't until 8.

DORIS
(not even looking at the Tech)
The dead don't do clocks, Plonk. You're late. You were always late.

Marrow flips over his tiny hourglass.

MARROW
Billing starts now.

DORIS
Let's start with the assets. I want the orb. I was there when it hatched.

The baby orb flickers. Its glow swings, slowly, to point right at the Tech.

ORB (V.O.)
Mama?

Everyone looks at the Tech.

PLONK
Actually, the dumbass IT support turned it off and on again, and now it thinks they're the mama.

DORIS
Well... you know what that means.

TECH
What does that mean?

Marrow clears his throat, which is impressive for someone without one.

MARROW
Marrow, of Marrow & Marrow, counsel for the deceased. Under the law of the dead, whoever the orb calls mama becomes a legal party to the divorce.

Doris smiles with about half of her face.

DORIS
So it's a three-way now.

PLONK
I've been in a three-way, Doris. This is worse.

The orb nudges against the Tech's sleeve.

ORB (V.O.)
Mama, what's a three-way?

Nobody answers.

A strip of paper CHUGS out from under the orb, like a receipt. The Tech tears it off and reads.

INSERT - THE RECEIPT

AFTERLIFE FAMILY COURT. TODAY AT NOON. PROPERTY IN DISPUTE: ONE (1) ORB. ONE (1) SILVERLIGHT CAPE.

BACK TO SCENE

TECH
(to the laptop)
Why do you even want the orb?

Doris leans so close to her camera we can see right up her nose. Which is to say, right into her skull.

DORIS
The orb is the only clean line between the living and the dead, sweetie. Ouija boards are full of perverts.
(sniffs)
I want the orb, and I want the Silverlight cape. And I want you on the stand at noon, telling the judge that Plonk is an unfit orb father.

TECH
What do I get?

DORIS
I know people down here. I can get your ticket queue cleared.
(beat)
Forever.

The Tech goes very still. Somewhere, faintly, angels sing.

Behind the Tech, Plonk sets down his mead, very slowly.

PLONK
Don't you fucking dare.

The Tech looks at Doris. Looks at Plonk. Looks at the baby orb, glowing up at them.

TECH
Doris. Go fuck yourself.

Long silence. Marrow's little hourglass keeps running.

DORIS
Well. See you both in court.

She hangs up. The laptop goes black.

The Tech turns around. Plonk is crying. He pulls the Tech into a hug.

PLONK
(whispering)
Nobody's ever said that to her. Not in three hundred years. Not even the plague.

He lets go, wipes his nose on his sleeve.

PLONK (CONT'D)
We need a plan.

TECH
You don't need a plan. You need to go make it right with her.

Plonk opens his mouth to argue. Nothing comes out. He looks at the orb.

ORB (V.O.)
Mama's right.

CUT TO:

EXT. CEMETERY - SUNSET

Golden hour. A crooked headstone in the grass:

DORIS. BELOVED WIFE. STILL MAD.

Plonk and the Tech stand in front of it. Plonk holds a bunch of very dead flowers. The cape hangs off his shoulders, humming.

PLONK
(re: the flowers)
They're for a dead woman. It's fine.

He sets them down. Clears his throat. Talks to the stone.

PLONK (CONT'D)
Forty years. I'm sorry. The stairs. And also I'm an asshole.

Nothing. Wind.

Then the ground GLOWS. Fog rolls in at ankle height, and DORIS rises up from behind the headstone, arms crossed.

She looks at Plonk for a long time. Then she looks at the cape.

PLONK (CONT'D)
(quietly)
If I take this off, I'm dust. Nine hundred years of dust, all at once.

DORIS
I know.

Plonk looks to the Tech, lost.

TECH
It's okay. Go.

Plonk looks at the Tech. He looks at Doris. Then he starts undoing the padlocks on the cape.

One. Two. Three.

JUMP CUT TO:

Doris, checking a wristwatch she does not have.

JUMP CUT TO:

The Tech, sitting on a neighbouring headstone.

JUMP CUT TO:

Plonk, on the last padlock.

PLONK
Fourteen.

He holds the cape out at arm's length, like a dirty diaper, and lets go. It drops into the grass.

Plonk's eyes go wide. His beard goes WHITE --

JUMP CUT TO:

-- GRAY --

JUMP CUT TO:

PLONK
Oh, shit. I forgot to feed the --

SMASH CUT TO:

A small pile of dust in a very old robe, with a wizard hat on top.

Silence.

The dust sneezes.

Plonk's GHOST steps out from behind the headstone, pale, blinking, dusting himself off. Doris is waiting.

She punches him in the arm. Hard.

Then she kisses him. It's gross. It's lovely. When they pull apart, a bit of her face has come off on his.

ACROSS THE CEMETERY

GARY (shirtless, ghostly, extremely defined abs) watches from behind a tree. He shrugs.

GARY
Gonna go visit my mom.

He wanders off.

BACK AT THE GRAVE

A PIGEON stands on top of the headstone. Plonk and Doris hold hands in front of it. The Tech stands to one side, holding the dead flowers like a bouquet.

PLONK
Doris. You are the worst thing that ever happened to me.

DORIS
You are a cheap, smelly old man and I have hated every year of it.

PLONK
I do.

DORIS
I do.

The pigeon coos. That's good enough.

The Tech starts a slow clap. Nobody joins in.

CUT TO:

EXT. TECH'S FRONT DOOR - DAY

A week later. The Tech opens the mailbox and pulls out a dusty envelope. The postmark reads THE AFTERLIFE.

INSERT - THE LETTER

Two kinds of handwriting, one shaky and one loopy.

PLONK (V.O.)
To the dumbass IT support. We leave you the tower,

DORIS (V.O.)
all nine hundred of its stairs,

PLONK (V.O.)
the orb,

DORIS (V.O.)
and the Silverlight cape, which neither of us needs anymore.

At the bottom, underlined twice, in both hands at once:

PLONK AND DORIS (V.O.)
Don't update anything.

CUT TO:

INT. WIZARD TOWER - DAY

Cleaner now. Sunlight. The Tech sits at the desk with a fresh coffee. The orb sits on its cushion, glowing a steady, healthy pink.

TECH
(to the orb)
How are we doing?

ORB (V.O.)
Good, Mama.

A little box pops up across the surface of the orb: AN UPDATE IS AVAILABLE.

The Tech taps it away without looking.

The Silverlight cape hangs on a coat hook. The Tech takes it down and swings it on. It hums. The Tech stands a little straighter, flexes a hand, looks at it.

The Tech feels like they could live forever. And slowly, the face falls, because they realize they will.

The WORK CRYSTAL on the desk, a glowing rock on a lanyard, BUZZES.

The Tech picks it up.

DEB (V.O.)
Hey, it's Deb from dispatch. New ticket for you.

The Tech looks out the window. Looks at the orb. Sips the coffee. Grimaces. Lukewarm.

TECH
Forever is a long time to do tech support.

SMASH CUT TO BLACK.

ORB (V.O.)
Mama, what's a three-way?

> THE END <
